{
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Historical U.S. Regular Gasoline Prices, 1930-2026",
    "country": "United States",
    "geographic_scope": "U.S. national average",
    "currency": "USD",
    "unit": "dollars per U.S. gallon",
    "price_basis": "Nominal/current dollars; not adjusted for inflation",
    "price_includes_taxes": true,
    "fuel_grade": "Regular gasoline",
    "methodology_notes": [
      "The historical series reports regular leaded gasoline through 1989 and regular unleaded gasoline beginning in 1990.",
      "1930-1991 values are taken from the Oak Ridge National Laboratory historical table and retain its published precision of $0.01.",
      "1992-2025 values use the EIA annual U.S. Regular All Formulations series. EIA annual averages are simple averages of weekly observations.",
      "EIA reports no complete annual averages for 1990 and 1991 in its current weekly-derived annual series because weekly data were not collected across part of that period; those two years therefore use the historical ORNL table.",
      "2026 is not a completed year. Its value is a year-to-date mean of EIA weekly observations through 2026-11-23, not a full-year average.",
      "Because the source series and collection methods differ, treat the 1991-1992 transition as a source/method change when comparing year-to-year movements."
    ],
